WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:06.340
The SCP Foundation faces off against a number
of incomprehensible, impossibly dangerous

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.180
threats every single day.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:13.460
They’ve gotten so used to containing terrifying
monsters and world-ending anomalies that it’s

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.610
really just all in a day’s work for them.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:20.920
But what if there was something that scared
even the most jaded Foundation personnel?

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.370
Something that none of them could track, understand,
or even see?

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:31.320
In the 1990s, employees of the SCP Foundation
began to disappear without a trace.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:36.620
At first, the higher-ups assumed it was traumatized
personnel making a break for it after they’d

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:38.829
seen something that finally made them snap.

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:41.450
But that wouldn’t account for all the blood.

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:46.340
At the site of every disappearance, the last
place anyone saw the missing person before

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:50.040
they were gone, there was a massive amount
of blood left behind.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:55.370
Not an “I cut my thumb while chopping onions”
amount of blood, but an “I’m missing a

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:57.559
limb” amount of blood.

00:00:57.559 --> 00:01:01.989
Buckets and buckets of what was confirmed
to be the missing person’s blood were found,

00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:05.650
spilled all over the scene of their disappearance.

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:10.440
The first recorded instance of this phenomenon
was captured via security footage of a laboratory

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:11.540
late at night.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:16.450
There, Dr. Porter was sat in his lab chair
finishing up some tests, running potentially

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:19.710
anomalous soil samples through a variety of
machines.

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:24.060
The room was mostly dark, save for the light
of a small desk lamp.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:27.880
Suddenly, he looked up from his work, eyes
darting around the room.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:33.340
He couldn’t see anything, but he could feel
it: there was something in there with him.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:37.650
He couldn’t shake the feeling that something
horrible was about to happen, and, not about

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:41.720
to stick around and see what it would be,
he made a break for the door.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:46.240
Just before his outstretched arm reached the
handle, he jerked back into the room as if

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:47.990
pulled by the back of his hair.

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:52.150
He looked around wildly for his assailant,
but there was nothing there that he could

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:53.150
see.

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:56.979
The security footage showed him jerked around,
thrashing his arms as he tried to fight off

00:01:56.979 --> 00:01:59.630
an invisible attacker for several seconds.

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:04.700
Then, he was gone, and the pristine white
tile of the laboratory was smeared with that

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:06.620
tell-tale bright red.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:10.910
He wasn’t pulled into a pocket dimension
like an attack by SCP-106.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:17.000
He was simply there one moment and gone the
next, the blood on the ground the only sign

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.239
he had ever been there at all.

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:23.470
Dr. Porter’s disappearance was troubling,
but the Foundation hoped it might just be

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:25.450
an isolated incident.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:30.090
Of course, nothing ever goes the way you’d
hope when you’re dealing with SCPs, and

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:34.950
within the next six months, three more personnel
had vanished in the same way.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:39.620
The phenomenon, whatever was causing it, had
a few simple rules it seemed to play by: it

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:44.850
occurred on a cycle of 1 to 3 months, it only
happened to Foundation personnel, and it always

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:48.989
happened in a dark place where visibility
was limited.

00:02:48.989 --> 00:02:54.310
Understandably unsettled, many personnel stopped
coming into work, afraid they might be next.

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:59.099
Unfortunately for them, the phenomenon was
not limited to the area within the Foundation’s

00:02:59.099 --> 00:03:00.099
walls.

00:03:00.099 --> 00:03:05.440
It could find them no matter how far they
ran, as soon as they were in the dark.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:12.000
You can’t fight, outrun, or outsmart the
setting sun or your bedside lamp going dead.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.980
Research Assistant Sanchez vanished while
taking a shortcut down an alley at night.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:19.280
Doctor Costanza was taken while she was reading
a book before bed.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:23.900
Her blood-stained sheets, discovered days
later, indicated she didn’t even have time

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.080
to run.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:29.250
Junior Researcher Watanabe disappeared from
the back row of a midnight screening of Evil

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:30.440
Dead 2.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:34.401
Moviegoers at the same screening reported
hearing some commotion from the back, like

00:03:34.401 --> 00:03:37.010
someone hitting one of the seats and kicking
their legs.

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:41.640
but they assumed it was just a massive Bruce
Campbell fan excited about the movie.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:44.790
The noise only lasted for a few seconds, anyway.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:49.660
And so the pattern continued, and every couple
of months one member of the Foundation staff

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:53.540
vanished, leaving behind only blood and a
sense of dread.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:58.040
None of the missing staff, dead or alive,
were ever found.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:04.530
The phenomenon was assigned the designation
SCP-835-JP, and, though they tried to come

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:09.200
up with a plan to contain it or put a stop
to it, many accepted it as simply another

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:14.390
occupational hazard in an increasingly long
list that came with doing the Foundation’s

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:15.390
work.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:19.120
Just when it was beginning to look like there
would never be a way to prevent new brushes

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:26.240
with SCP-835 short of never being alone in
the dark ever again, something weird and wonderful

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:27.240
happened.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:32.080
In a Japanese SCP Foundation facility, during
one of the phenomenon’s inactive periods,

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:38.839
a booklet entitled “Artist’s Impression
of SCP-835-JP” was found on the desk of

00:04:38.839 --> 00:04:39.889
a research assistant.

00:04:39.889 --> 00:04:46.089
It depicted a fictional character known as
Keteru Yamiko, intended to be a personification

00:04:46.089 --> 00:04:47.159
of the phenomena.

00:04:47.159 --> 00:04:52.900
Keteru Yamiko, as depicted in the booklet,
is a young woman drawn in a traditional anime

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.490
and manga art style.

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:59.729
She is pale, with blue eyes and long black
hair, and is dressed in a classic Japanese

00:04:59.729 --> 00:05:01.009
school uniform.

00:05:01.009 --> 00:05:05.199
In addition to her design, the booklet also
described the character’s abilities and

00:05:05.199 --> 00:05:06.199
backstory.

00:05:06.199 --> 00:05:11.379
Keteru is described as a type of assassin,
with expertise in predatory ambush.

00:05:11.379 --> 00:05:14.199
A santoku knife is her weapon of choice.

00:05:14.199 --> 00:05:18.270
She also displays anomalous abilities with
regard to the absence of light.

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:22.860
She is able to manipulate darkness, and use
dark and shadows as a weapon that she can

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:24.610
trap her targets with.

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:29.889
She is also able to teleport using shadows,
transporting herself, objects, or her prey

00:05:29.889 --> 00:05:33.300
through shadows to remove all evidence of
what she has done.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:37.690
The origins of Keteru’s abilities are somewhat
murky, but whether she was born with them

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:42.630
or given them, she came into her unusual talents
at a young age.

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:49.350
Due to her abilities, she was found by a mysterious
organization, an unknown enemy of the SCP

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:52.270
Foundation, and abducted by them as a child.

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:57.270
There, they indoctrinated her and trained
her to be a master assassin, teaching her

00:05:57.270 --> 00:06:02.949
how to use her abilities, master hand-to-hand
combat and the use of weapons, and to have

00:06:02.949 --> 00:06:05.729
the ice-cold demeanor of a perfect killer.

00:06:05.729 --> 00:06:10.869
She learned to move in the shadows and make
darkness her ultimate home and ally.

00:06:10.869 --> 00:06:15.469
Once her training was complete, Keteru was
sent out into the world with one mission:

00:06:15.469 --> 00:06:20.289
To take out members of the SCP Foundation
by any means necessary.

00:06:20.289 --> 00:06:24.659
According to the lore of the booklet, her
killings drew the attention of the Foundation,

00:06:24.659 --> 00:06:29.050
though they did not understand who she was
or who had sent her.

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:34.370
Then, they assigned her the designation of
SCP-835-JP.

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:38.770
The booklet was sent to the site’s head
researcher, who brought in the assistant for

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:40.120
further questioning.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:44.300
The man confessed to having drawn the booklet,
saying that drawing Keteru Yamiko had made

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:47.369
him feel less afraid of the mysterious entity.

00:06:47.369 --> 00:06:52.179
By turning it into a fictional character,
he was taking his sense of control back as

00:06:52.179 --> 00:06:57.259
well as turning his fear into a chance to
explore his favorite hobby, drawing.

00:06:57.259 --> 00:07:02.689
What had once been a completely unknown enemy,
something without a face or a motive of any

00:07:02.689 --> 00:07:07.999
kind, was now a classic anime character and
something he could wrap his mind around.

00:07:07.999 --> 00:07:10.400
Also, he just thought it all looked really
cool.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:14.499
He was reprimanded for drawing on the job
and making light of a phenomenon that had

00:07:14.499 --> 00:07:19.169
taken so many of his colleagues, he was transferred
to a different department, and the booklet

00:07:19.169 --> 00:07:20.759
was largely forgotten about.

00:07:20.759 --> 00:07:25.800
At least, until one researcher, Dr. Sato,
noticed something curious.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:31.699
After the discovery of the Keteru Yamiko booklet,
also known as Incident-835-JP, there were

00:07:31.699 --> 00:07:34.729
no disappearances for five months.

00:07:34.729 --> 00:07:38.919
Another disappearance finally occurred, but
the pattern, which had been so consistent

00:07:38.919 --> 00:07:42.309
before, was disrupted for the first time in
a decade.

00:07:42.309 --> 00:07:47.709
Dr. Sato noticed this delay, and, though his
colleagues mocked him for it, drew a connection

00:07:47.709 --> 00:07:52.840
between the longer inactive period and the
discovery of the Keteru Yamiko booklet.

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:58.399
He quickly got to work, and developed and
proposed Protocol Idol-835, which was approved

00:07:58.399 --> 00:08:03.520
by a head researcher desperate for some kind
of solution, and promptly put into practice.

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:11.099
Dr. Sato’s theory behind the implementation
of Protocol Idol was that, somehow, SCP-835-JP

00:08:11.099 --> 00:08:15.569
was connected to and influenced by the perceptions
of the Foundation personnel.

00:08:15.569 --> 00:08:20.899
In fact, it had likely originated from their
collective sense of anxiety and paranoia in

00:08:20.899 --> 00:08:27.289
the first place, acting as a tulpa, or a thought
made real through intense concentration and

00:08:27.289 --> 00:08:28.289
belief.

00:08:28.289 --> 00:08:32.380
Therefore, he hypothesized that by changing
the staff’s perception of the phenomena

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:38.080
from something horrifying and unknowable to
an approachable and even fun fictional character,

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:42.349
they could somehow contain it and stop any
further disappearances.

00:08:42.349 --> 00:08:48.230
The goal of Protocol Idol was to create a
shared version of SCP-835-JP for all of the

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:52.970
staff to focus on, stripping the entity of
its original power.

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:57.589
Since many staff had already seen the original
Keteru Yamiko booklet, she was chosen to be

00:08:57.589 --> 00:09:01.019
the shared, agreed-upon description of SCP-835-JP.

00:09:01.019 --> 00:09:06.519
With all of that decided, the Protocol was
officially put into place.

00:09:06.519 --> 00:09:12.040
First, all of the documents and reports that
referred to SCP-835-JP were edited to include

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:17.190
details about Keteru Yamiko, including descriptions
of the character, repeated mentions of her

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:21.490
name instead of the SCP’s number, and various
illustrations.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:26.079
In addition to changing the records, a publicity
campaign was mounted to cement the idea of

00:09:26.079 --> 00:09:29.149
Keteru Yamiko in the minds of all of the staff.

00:09:29.149 --> 00:09:34.560
Keteru Yamiko’s design was painted on various
supplies, on the side of transport vans, on

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:39.420
the doors to laboratories, and as murals on
several walls throughout the facility.

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:44.440
The booklet was copied and distributed around
the facility as a piece of required reading.

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:48.620
The original author of the booklet was brought
back on board to design and head the creation

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:54.300
of a variety of other reading materials, including
fictional novels, manga, and short animated

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:57.920
videos featuring Keteru Yamiko as the main
character.

00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:02.360
Mandatory watch parties were held for these
short animations, and free snacks and drinks

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:05.209
were provided in order to boost morale.

00:10:05.209 --> 00:10:10.500
Several employees began jokingly referring
to these watch parties as “SCP Foundation

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:11.710
Anime Club.”

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:16.050
Through the efforts of the Idol Protocol,
the image and knowledge of Keteru Yamiko spread

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:22.490
throughout the Foundation and became the dominant
perception of SCP-835-JP.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:26.430
Since the implementation of this protocol,
there have been no disappearances in line

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:32.190
with SCP-835-JP’s pattern, and the project
was declared a success.

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:41.120
Dr. Sato included this note in SCP-835-JP’s
file: “SCP-835-JP is probably a manifestation

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:46.430
of the instinctive fear that something threatening
oneself may be lurking in the darkness.

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:51.420
But the imaginary monster we once feared has
now been reduced to a clichéd character with

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:53.920
Protocol Idol-835.”

00:10:53.920 --> 00:11:01.290
Ever since the implementation of Protocol
Idol-835, SCP-835-JP is considered neutralized.

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:04.519
Its classification has been downgraded from
Keter to Safe.

00:11:04.519 --> 00:11:08.139
There have been talks about strengthening
the entity’s containment by expanding the

00:11:08.139 --> 00:11:12.519
protocol outside of the Foundation, in order
to prevent the possibility of containment

00:11:12.519 --> 00:11:17.839
breaches down the line that might be brought
on by exposure to a major cognitohazard or

00:11:17.839 --> 00:11:19.560
in-house amnestics.

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:24.009
A special team of illustrators, animators,
and writers has been brought on to spearhead

00:11:24.009 --> 00:11:29.519
the protocol, creating additional comic books,
posters, and even beginning the early stages

00:11:29.519 --> 00:11:35.879
of production on a feature-length animated
film about SCP-835-JP and her various exploits,

00:11:35.879 --> 00:11:39.759
tentatively titled “Keteru Yamiko: Shadow
Girl”.

00:11:39.759 --> 00:11:44.649
There have been no plans made yet for international
distribution, but who knows?

00:11:44.649 --> 00:11:48.870
We might just see Keteru Yamiko on the big
screen one of these days.

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:54.370
She might just end up as the first ever SCP
to become a mainstream celebrity.

00:11:54.370 --> 00:11:58.649
And until then, the Foundation could also
disseminate knowledge about her through other

00:11:58.649 --> 00:11:59.649
means.

00:11:59.649 --> 00:12:02.170
Say, a fun little animated YouTube video.

00:12:02.170 --> 00:12:06.269
But what’s the chance they’d ever pull
a move like that, right?

00:12:06.269 --> 00:12:13.819
Now go check out “SCP-2935 O, Death and
More Epic SCP Stories You Can't Miss” and

00:12:13.819 --> 00:12:19.290
“Procedure 110 Montauk REVEALED - Fear Alone
- SCP-231 Tale” for more mind-bending anomalous

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:21.449
action from the SCP Foundation!

